---
/* =========================================================================================
   THE LIQUIDATION MAP, NOW: WHAT IS STANDING AT EACH PRICE, AND WHAT A MOVE WOULD CLOSE.

   WHY A SECOND PICTURE ON A PAGE THAT HAS ONE. The heatmap answers "where did levels sit over
   the window, and which did price take out". A trader who searches "liquidation map" is asking
   something narrower: from here, how much gets closed if price goes to X? CoinGlass answers it
   behind a login (checked 15 October 2026: its Liquidation Map opens a "Log in to unlock full
   data" dialog). This answers it on the open page, from the same model as the heatmap.

   PRICE RUNS UP THE PAGE, AS ON THE HEATMAP ABOVE IT, NOT ALONG IT. A price-on-X bar chart is
   wider than a phone and would scroll sideways like every other chart here; a ladder is tall and
   narrow, fits 375px without scrolling, and lines up with the heatmap's own price axis, so a band
   on one is a bar on the other at the same height.

   THE GUIDE LINES ARE THE READING. At one, two, five and ten percent each way the line carries the
   cumulative notional a move to it would close — the figure the picture exists to give, printed
   where the eye already is rather than on a second axis. The same eight figures are in the table
   beside it as text, because a picture is not an answer an extractor or a screen reader can use.

   MODELLED, AND SAID SO ON THE PICTURE ITSELF. The bars are the heatmap's right-hand column re-
   binned (levelsView in src/lib/liqmap.ts): the same assumptions, nothing added. Levels outside the
   drawn price range are not in it, and the share they hold is printed with the reads.

   COLOUR IS LEVERAGE, FROM THE DENSITY RAMP. Side needs no hue — it is above or below the mark,
   labelled on the picture — so the four reserved hues (candle up/down, funding direction) stay
   unused, which the colour-language check would otherwise refuse.

   THE READER'S OWN PRICE IS THE PART A CHAT ANSWER CANNOT CARRY. The eight standard moves are
   figures an assistant can lift and repeat; "what if it goes to 78,500" is a question about a
   price nobody published. So the page takes one: ?at= is read on the server and answered in the
   first response — a line on the ladder and a sentence in the reads — and the GET form beside it
   works with scripting off. With scripting on, a press or drag on the ladder moves that line and
   rewrites the sentence and the address, so the reading a reader arrives at is a link they can
   send. The figure is never the script's own: the server publishes the rows it summed
   (data-curve) and both sides read them through cumulativeAt()/atReading() in public/shared.js.
   ========================================================================================= */
import type { LevelsView, LevelBin } from "../lib/liqmap.ts";
import { utcStamp } from "../lib/freshness.ts";
import { RAMP, INK, MONO, SANS, compact } from "../lib/chart.ts";
import { pct, usd, axisDp } from "../lib/funding.ts";
import { signedPct, atReading, cumulativeAt } from "../../public/shared.js";

interface Props {
  view: LevelsView;
  symbol: string;
  /** decimals for prices on this page — the axis precision, the same the script formats with */
  dp: number;
  clipped: number;
  /** the reader's own price from ?at=, already parsed; null when absent or unreadable */
  at: number | null;
  /** what the reader typed when it could not be read, so the page can say so */
  atRaw: string | null;
  /** where the form submits, and the view it must keep (profile, window) */
  action: string;
  carry: [string, string][];
  /** the same model a day earlier on the same price rows (mapModel's `then`), or null */
  then: { levels: LevelsView; candlesTo: number; oiAt: number; cleared: number } | null;
}
const { view, symbol, dp, clipped, at, atRaw, action, carry, then } = Astro.props;
const fmt = (v: number) => usd(v, dp);
/* The ladder's own price labels and the mark pill are an axis, and keep the shorter axis precision. */
const afmt = (v: number) => usd(v, axisDp(view.mark));

/* 440 UNITS, DRAWN 1:1 ON A WIDE SCREEN. At 640 a 375px phone scaled the ladder to half and its
   labels to seven pixels (15 October 2026); a second, phone-width copy would have pushed
   /liquidations past its weight budget, so the one ladder is narrower: about nine pixels on a phone,
   true size beside the reads. The title, the leverage key and the side label each have a row. */
/* FULL WIDTH, AND THE TEXT STAYS TWELVE PIXELS (15 October 2026, the owner's call: the ladder is
   the page's picture and deserves the column). One ladder, not a wide and a phone copy — a second
   copy is 8 KB the /liquidations budget does not have. So the drawing is split by what may stretch:
   the bars, ghosts, guides and lines are one svg in a 1000-unit box drawn preserveAspectRatio=none,
   which stretches across the column and only across it; the price labels, the mark pill and the
   guide labels are fixed-size layers on its left and right edges, on the same pixel rows. Rows are
   13px at every width, and the header keeps its 440-unit drawing. */
const W = 440, padT = 80, rowH = 13;
const labelW = 84, plotL = labelW, X = 1000;
const bins = view.bins;
/* The plot box: 12px above the top row and below the bottom one, for the pills that sit on an edge. */
const top0 = 12;
const plotH = bins.length * rowH;
const PH = plotH + 2 * top0;
const lo = bins[0].lo, hi = bins[bins.length - 1].hi;
const y = (p: number) => Math.round((top0 + ((hi - p) / (hi - lo)) * plotH) * 10) / 10;
/* One scale for both runs, so a ghost longer than its bar means the level was heavier a day ago. */
const peak = Math.max(view.peakBin, then ? then.levels.peakBin : 0);
const xLen = (n: number) => (n / peak) * X;
const sideSum = (b: LevelBin, mark: number) => (b.mid < mark ? b.longSum : b.shortSum);
/* Lower leverage darker, higher brighter: the rungs that liquidate soonest catch the eye first. */
const levColor = (li: number) => RAMP[Math.round(11 + (10 * li) / Math.max(1, view.levs.length - 1))];
const markY = y(view.mark);
/* Price labels every few bins, skipping the ones that would collide with the mark pill. */
const labelEvery = Math.max(1, Math.round(bins.length / 12));
const guides = view.moves.filter((m) => m.price > lo && m.price < hi);
const fromMark = (p: number) => signedPct((p - view.mark) / view.mark);
/* The reader's line, clamped to the picture: a price past the edge sits on the edge, and the
   sentence says it is past it. */
const atY = at === null ? null : Math.min(top0 + plotH, Math.max(top0, y(at)));
const atCum = at === null ? null : view.cumAt(at);
const atLabel = (price: number, c: { side: string; notional: number }) =>
  `${fmt(price)} → ${compact(c.notional)} ${c.side === "long" ? "longs" : "shorts"}`;
const reading = at === null ? null : atReading(view.curve, view.mark, at, view.lo, view.hi, dp, then ? then.levels.curve : null);
const example = fmt(view.mark * 0.95);
const curveJson = JSON.stringify({
  curve: view.curve, mark: view.mark, lo: view.lo, hi: view.hi, dp,
  y0: top0, h: plotH, top: hi, bottom: lo,
  then: then ? then.levels.curve : null,
});
/* THE DAY'S CHANGE IN WORDS, within 5% each side of the mark — the band a trader reads first — from
   the same rows the table and the ghosts are drawn from. */
const band5 = then ? (["long", "short"] as const).map((side) => {
  const price = view.mark * (side === "long" ? 0.95 : 1.05);
  return { side, now: cumulativeAt(view.curve, view.mark, price).notional, was: cumulativeAt(then.levels.curve, view.mark, price).notional };
}) : [];
const moved = (now: number, was: number) =>
  was > 0 ? `${now >= was ? "up" : "down"} from ${compact(was)} to ${compact(now)} (${signedPct(now / was - 1, 0)})` : now > 0 ? `up from none to ${compact(now)}` : "none, as a day earlier";
const tip = (i: number) => {
  const b = bins[i];
  const side = b.mid < view.mark ? "long" : "short";
  const sideN = side === "long" ? b.longSum : b.shortSum;
  const cum = view.cumAt(b.mid);
  const rows = view.levs
    .map((L, li) => [L, side === "long" ? b.long[li] : b.short[li]] as const)
    .filter(([, n]) => n > 0)
    .map(([L, n]) => `<span>${L}×</span><b>${compact(n)}</b>`).join("");
  return `<div class="tip__h">${fmt(b.lo)} – ${fmt(b.hi)} · ${fromMark(b.mid)}</div>` +
    `<div class="tip__g"><span>${side === "long" ? "Longs" : "Shorts"} closed here</span><b>${compact(sideN)}</b>${rows}` +
    `<span>A move to here closes</span><b>${compact(cum.notional)}</b>` +
    (then ? `<span>Here a day earlier</span><b>${compact(sideSum(then.levels.bins[i], view.mark))}</b>` : "") + `</div>`;
};
/* Every bar segment is computed here rather than in the markup: Astro's compiler reads a bare
   comparison inside an expression in the template as the start of a tag. */
const rowsOut = bins.map((b, i) => {
  const yt = y(b.hi);
  const parts = b.mid < view.mark ? b.long : b.short;
  let x = 0;
  const segs: { x: number; w: number; fill: string }[] = [];
  parts.forEach((n, li) => {
    if (!(n > 0)) return;
    const w = xLen(n);
    segs.push({ x, w: Math.max(1.5, w), fill: levColor(li) });
    x += w;
  });
  const showLabel = i % labelEvery === 0 && Math.abs(y(b.mid) - markY) > 14;
  const ghost = then ? xLen(sideSum(then.levels.bins[i], view.mark)) : 0;
  return {
    yt, h: Math.max(1, y(b.lo) - y(b.hi) - 1), hit: Math.max(1, y(b.lo) - y(b.hi)),
    segs, tip: tip(i), label: showLabel ? afmt(b.mid) : "", ly: y(b.mid) + 4, ghost,
  };
});
/* WHICH SIDE THE LADDER LEANS TO, as a ratio a reader can carry away, rather than two totals to divide. */
const sideWords = (() => {
  const s = view.totalShort, l = view.totalLong;
  if (!(s > 0) && !(l > 0)) return "Nothing modelled stands within the drawn range.";
  if (!(s > 0) || !(l > 0)) return `Only ${s > 0 ? "shorts" : "longs"} stand within the drawn range: ${compact(s > 0 ? s : l)}.`;
  const r = s >= l ? s / l : l / s;
  const heavy = s >= l ? `shorts above the mark (${compact(s)}) outweigh longs below it (${compact(l)})` : `longs below the mark (${compact(l)}) outweigh shorts above it (${compact(s)})`;
  return r < 1.1 ? `Shorts above the mark (${compact(s)}) and longs below it (${compact(l)}) stand roughly level within the drawn range.` : `Within the drawn range ${heavy}, ${r.toFixed(1)} to 1.`;
})();
---
<figure class="levels" data-levels={curveJson}>
  <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${W} ${padT}`} class="levels__head">
    <text x="12" y="22" fill={INK.dim} font-size="12" font-family={MONO} letter-spacing="1">MODELLED · STANDING NOW</text>
    {/* the leverage key, on the picture rather than under it */}
    {view.levs.map((L, li) => (
      <g>
        <rect x={12 + li * 56} y="33" width="13" height="13" rx="3" fill={levColor(li)} />
        <text x={12 + li * 56 + 18} y="44.5" fill={INK.dim} font-size="12.5" font-family={MONO}>{L}×</text>
      </g>
    ))}
    <text x={plotL} y="68" fill={INK.faint} font-size="12.5" font-family={SANS}>shorts closed above ↑</text>
    {then && (
      <g>
        {/* A flat outlined bar, the ghost's own shape: a 14×11 square beside words read as an
            unticked checkbox (seen on /liquidations/eth, 15 October 2026). */}
        <rect x={W - 120} y="60.5" width="24" height="7" fill="none" stroke={INK.neutral} stroke-width="1" opacity="0.55" />
        <text x={W - 90} y="68" fill={INK.dim} font-size="12.5" font-family={SANS}>a day earlier</text>
      </g>
    )}
  </svg>
  <div class="levels__plot" style={`height:${PH}px`}>
    <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${X} ${PH}`} preserveAspectRatio="none" role="img" data-tips class="levels__svg" style={`height:${PH}px`}
         aria-label={`Modelled liquidation levels for ${symbol} by price, longs below the mark and shorts above. The figures are in the table below it.`}>
      {rowsOut.map((r) => (
        <g>
          {r.segs.map((g) => <rect x={g.x} y={r.yt} width={g.w} height={r.h} fill={g.fill} />)}
          {r.ghost > 0.5 && <rect x="0" y={r.yt + 0.5} width={r.ghost} height={Math.max(0, r.h - 1)} fill="none" stroke={INK.neutral} stroke-width="1" opacity="0.55" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke" />}
          <rect x="0" y={r.yt} width={X} height={r.hit} fill="transparent" data-tip={r.tip} />
        </g>
      ))}
      {guides.map((g) => (
        <line x1="0" x2={X} y1={y(g.price)} y2={y(g.price)} stroke={INK.dim} stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="3 4" opacity="0.55" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke" pointer-events="none" />
      ))}
      <line x1="0" x2={X} y1={markY} y2={markY} stroke={INK.acc} stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="2 4" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke" pointer-events="none" />
      {/* THE READER'S PRICE. Drawn by the server when ?at= is set; the script moves it, and keeps it
          hidden until the first press when there is none. Its label is the HTML pill below. */}
      <g data-at-line pointer-events="none" display={atY === null ? "none" : undefined} transform={`translate(0 ${atY ?? top0})`}>
        <line x1="0" x2={X} y1="0" y2="0" stroke={INK.neutral} stroke-width="1.5" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke" />
      </g>
    </svg>
    <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${labelW} ${PH}`} class="levels__axis" style={`height:${PH}px`}>
      {rowsOut.map((r) => r.label && <text x={labelW - 10} y={r.ly} fill={INK.faint} font-size="12" font-family={MONO} text-anchor="end">{r.label}</text>)}
      <rect x="2" y={markY - 11} width={labelW - 6} height="22" rx="5" fill={INK.acc} />
      <text x={2 + (labelW - 6) / 2} y={markY + 4.5} fill={INK.accInk} font-size="12.5" font-weight="600" font-family={MONO} text-anchor="middle">{afmt(view.mark)}</text>
    </svg>
    <svg viewBox={`0 0 180 ${PH}`} class="levels__guides" style={`height:${PH}px`}>
      {guides.map((g) => (
        <g>
          <rect x="8" y={y(g.price) - 11} width="170" height="20" rx="5" fill="#0f1215" opacity="0.92" />
          <text x="168" y={y(g.price) + 4} fill={INK.neutral} font-size="12.5" font-family={MONO} text-anchor="end">
            {signedPct(g.pct, 0)} → {compact(g.notional)} {g.side === "long" ? "longs" : "shorts"}
          </text>
        </g>
      ))}
    </svg>
    <span class="levels__atpill" data-at-pill hidden={atY === null} style={`top:${atY ?? top0}px`}><span data-at-label>{at !== null && atCum ? atLabel(at, atCum) : ""}</span></span>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="levels__foot">longs closed below ↓</figcaption>
</figure>

<div class="levels__reads">
  {/* A GET form, so it works with scripting off; the script reads the field as it is typed. */}
  <form method="GET" action={action} class="levels__at" data-at-form>
    <label for="levels-at" class="levels__atlabel">Your price — what a move to it would close</label>
    <div class="levels__atrow">
      {carry.map(([k, v]) => <input type="hidden" name={k} value={v} />)}
      <input id="levels-at" class="field" name="at" type="text" inputmode="decimal" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false"
             value={atRaw ?? (at !== null ? String(at) : "")} placeholder={`e.g. ${example}`} data-at-input />
      <button class="btn btn--primary" type="submit">Read</button>
    </div>
    <p class="levels__atout" data-at-out aria-live="polite">{
      reading ?? (atRaw ? `“${atRaw}” is not a price this page can read. Enter one like ${example}.` : "Type a price, or press the ladder. The link keeps your reading.")
    }</p>
  </form>
  <div class="levels__figures">
  <table class="tbl levels__tbl">
    <caption>If {symbol} moves from {fmt(view.mark)}: modelled notional closed on the way</caption>
    <thead><tr><th class="num">Move</th><th class="num">To</th><th class="num">Closed</th>{then && <th class="num">A day earlier</th>}</tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {[...view.moves].sort((a, b) => b.pct - a.pct).map((m) => (
        <tr><td class="num">{signedPct(m.pct, 0)}</td><td class="num">{fmt(m.price)}</td><td class="num">{compact(m.notional)}{m.beyond && <sup class="levels__past" title="past the drawn range">†</sup>}</td>{then && <td class="num levels__was">{compact(cumulativeAt(then.levels.curve, view.mark, m.price).notional)}</td>}</tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  {then && (
    <p class="levels__day">
      <b>Against a day earlier</b> (the outlined bars; candles to {utcStamp(then.candlesTo, 0)}, open interest
      read {utcStamp(then.oiAt, 0)}): longs within 5% below the mark are {moved(band5[0].now, band5[0].was)},
      shorts within 5% above {moved(band5[1].now, band5[1].was)}, and price cleared {compact(then.cleared)}.
    </p>
  )}
  <p class="levels__note">
    {sideWords} {pct(clipped)} of modelled notional sits beyond the drawn range and is not counted.
    {view.moves.some((m) => m.beyond) && <>{" "}† That move lands past the edge of the drawn range
    ({fmt(view.lo)} – {fmt(view.hi)}): the figure is every level of its side inside the range, and
    whatever stands beyond the edge is not in it.</>}
  </p>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  .levels { margin: 0; background: #0f1215; border-radius: 12px; padding: 0 0 10px; }
  .levels__head { display: block; width: 100%; max-width: 440px; height: auto; }
  .levels__plot { position: relative; }
  .levels__plot > svg { position: absolute; top: 0; display: block; }
  .levels__svg { left: 84px; width: calc(100% - 96px); }
  .levels__axis { left: 0; width: 84px; pointer-events: none; }
  .levels__guides { right: 12px; width: 180px; pointer-events: none; }
  .levels__atpill { position: absolute; left: 88px; transform: translateY(-50%); padding: 3px 8px; border-radius: 5px; font: 600 12.5px var(--mono); color: #0f1215; background: var(--text-dim); pointer-events: none; white-space: nowrap; max-width: calc(100% - 100px); overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; }
  .levels__foot { font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--text-faint); padding: 2px 0 0 84px; }
  /* Underneath the ladder: the reader's price beside the moves table where there is room for both. */
  .levels__reads { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 20px; align-items: start; }
  .levels__figures { min-width: 0; }
  @media (min-width: 1100px) { .levels__reads { grid-template-columns: minmax(300px, 420px) minmax(0, 1fr); } }
  .levels__svg { touch-action: pan-y; cursor: crosshair; }
  .levels__at { margin: 0 0 18px; padding: 14px 16px; border: 1px solid var(--border-soft); border-radius: 12px; background: var(--surface-1); }
  .levels__atlabel { display: block; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .levels__atrow { display: flex; gap: 8px; }
  .levels__atrow .field { flex: 1 1 auto; min-width: 0; }
  .levels__day { font-size: var(--fs-sm); line-height: 1.55; margin: 12px 0 0; }
  .levels__was { color: var(--text-dim); }
  .levels__past { color: var(--text-faint); margin-left: 2px; }
  .levels__atout { margin: 10px 0 0; font-size: var(--fs-sm); line-height: 1.5; }
  /* FOUR COLUMNS, SO IT FITS A PHONE. The day-earlier column put the table at 416px inside a 315px
     column and gave every liquidation page a sideways scroll at 375px (15 October 2026,
     scripts/phone-width.mjs). The Side column went rather than being hidden on phones: the sign of
     the move already says it, the caption says which sign is which, and text hidden at one width
     is text some readers never receive. */
  .levels__tbl th, .levels__tbl td { padding-left: 6px; padding-right: 6px; }
  .levels__tbl th { white-space: normal; }
  .levels__tbl caption { caption-side: top; text-align: left; font-size: var(--fs-sm); color: var(--text-dim); padding: 0 0 8px; }
  .levels__note { font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--text-faint); line-height: 1.55; margin: 10px 0 0; }
</style>
